{'sentiment score': 0, 'confidence': 1, 'reason': " Disclosure of supplemental cash flow information related to operating leases is required by the Accounting Standards Codification (ASC) 205, Communications - Disclosures of Supplemental Plan Information. The standard requires entities that issue debt securities or are required to issue debt securities in the future to disclose certain information about their plans for use of proceeds from debt securities. This includes supplemental cash flow information related to operating leases. The requirement applies to all entities that have outstanding public debt and is intended to provide investors with more timely and relevant information about an entity's liquidity position and its ability to meet its debt obligations. In this case, the supplemental cash flow information related to operating leases provides insight into the company's plans for using the proceeds from its lease payments to fund future capital expenditures or other purposes.", 'company_name': 'COMPANY CONFORMED NAME:\t\t\tAVITA Medical, Inc.'}